# 高频词汇 List08
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List08核心词汇

{{rational}}{/ˈræʃənl/}{理性的；合理的}{Consumers are becoming more rational in their spending habits.}}
{{recognize}}{/ˈrekəɡnaɪz/}{认出；承认}{The program recognizes outstanding contributions to science.}}
{{recommend}}{/ˌrekəˈmend/}{推荐；建议}{Experts recommend exercising at least 30 minutes a day.}}
{{recover}}{/rɪˈkʌvər/}{恢复；收回}{The economy took years to recover from the recession.}}
{{reduce}}{/rɪˈdjuːs/}{减少；降低}{The company aims to reduce its carbon footprint.}}
{{reflect}}{/rɪˈflekt/}{反映；反思}{The survey results reflect changing attitudes toward work.}}
{{reform}}{/rɪˈfɔːm/}{改革；改良}{Healthcare reform remains a contentious political issue.}}
{{regulate}}{/ˈreɡjuleɪt/}{管理；调节}{The industry needs to be more strictly regulated.}}
{{reject}}{/rɪˈdʒekt/}{拒绝；驳回}{The court rejected the appeal on procedural grounds.}}
{{relate}}{/rɪˈleɪt/}{联系；叙述}{The article relates economic growth to education levels.}}
{{release}}{/rɪˈliːs/}{释放；发布}{The government released the report on Friday.}}
{{relevant}}{/ˈreləvənt/}{相关的；切题的}{Please provide only information relevant to the inquiry.}}
{{rely}}{/rɪˈlaɪ/}{依赖；信赖}{Many rural communities rely on agriculture for their livelihood.}}
{{require}}{/rɪˈkwaɪər/}{要求；需要}{The position requires a minimum of two years' experience.}}
{{research}}{/rɪˈsɜːtʃ/}{研究；调查}{More research is needed to understand the long-term effects.}}
{{resist}}{/rɪˈzɪst/}{抵抗；抵制}{Some groups resisted the proposed changes to the law.}}
{{resolve}}{/rɪˈzɒlv/}{解决；决心}{The dispute was resolved through mediation.}}
{{resource}}{/rɪˈsɔːs/}{资源}{Water is a precious natural resource that must be protected.}}
{{respond}}{/rɪˈspɒnd/}{回应；反应}{The government responded swiftly to the crisis.}}
{{restore}}{/rɪˈstɔːr/}{恢复；修复}{Efforts are underway to restore the damaged ecosystem.}}
{{restrict}}{/rɪˈstrɪkt/}{限制；约束}{Access to the building is restricted to authorized personnel.}}
{{retain}}{/rɪˈteɪn/}{保留；保持}{The company uses bonuses to retain top talent.}}
{{reveal}}{/rɪˈviːl/}{揭示；透露}{The study revealed significant differences between the groups.}}
{{revenue}}{/ˈrevənjuː/}{收入；税收}{Advertising revenue has declined due to market changes.}}
{{reverse}}{/rɪˈvɜːs/}{逆转；相反}{The court reversed the lower court's decision.}}
{{schedule}}{/ˈʃedjuːl/}{时间表；安排}{The conference is scheduled for the first week of June.}}
{{secure}}{/sɪˈkjʊər/}{安全的；获得}{The company secured funding for its expansion plans.}}
{{select}}{/sɪˈlekt/}{选择；挑选}{Participants were selected based on their qualifications.}}
{{shift}}{/ʃɪft/}{转变；轮班}{There has been a cultural shift toward remote work.}}
{{significant}}{/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/}{重要的；显著的}{The discovery is significant for the field of genetics.}}
